		"habit": "open-grown mature tree 20 to 25 m tall, spread 20 to 30 m. Width about 1.5 to 1.7 times the height. Crown about 80 % of the height; clear trunk about 15 to 20 %, short and massive (1.5 to 2 m across at the flare). Widest a little below the middle of the crown. Outline a broad low irregular dome, its edge broken into clumps with sky between them. One trunk that forks low into several huge limbs.",
		"branching": "alternate. Limbs leave the trunk at wide angles, run out almost level and kink and twist between joints; the lowest limbs dip at their ends. About five orders from trunk to leaf. Twigs short, stiff and angular, buds crowded at the twig ends.",
		"leaves": "simple, 7 to 12 cm long, 4 to 7 cm wide (about 1.8 to 1), broadest above the middle. Four to five pairs of deep rounded lobes, no teeth, no bristle tips. Base with two small ear-like lobes on a very short stalk (under 1 cm). Pinnate veins. Dark green above, paler blue-green below.",
